<title>USA: N.Y. business loans rose $954 mln in Feb 19 week.</title>
<headline>N.Y. business loans rose $954 mln in Feb 19 week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commercial and industrial loans at the six major New York banks, excluding acceptances, rose $954 million to $44,560 million in the week ended February 19, the Federal Reserve Bank of New York said.</p>
<p>Including acceptances, loans rose $962 million to $44,804 million.</p>
<p>Commercial paper outstanding nationally rose $24 million to $812,630 million.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
